      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Great Northern Railway reached Monitor in 1892, sparking the construction of the Peshastin irrigation ditch that would flood the valley with water.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monitor%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the early 1900s the ditch was finished, and local orchards began thriving along the fertile Wenatchee River flats.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monitor%2C_Washington",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community sits 8 miles upstream from the Wenatchee River’s confluence with the Columbia, nestled in the lower Wenatchee Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
